WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.775
Try it.

2
00:00:00.775 --> 00:00:05.935
Lab 1 runs in the hr-lifecycle folder
of the examples, on fictional fixtures,

3
00:00:05.935 --> 00:00:09.763
and nothing in it signs in to
anything or sends a request.

4
00:00:09.763 --> 00:00:13.337
Step one lists what the scan
reads, and with what permission.

5
00:00:13.337 --> 00:00:16.932
The list option prints the task's
calls without making them:

6
00:00:16.932 --> 00:00:21.773
two GET calls against the audit logs,
the directory audits and the provisioning

7
00:00:21.773 --> 00:00:26.100
logs, which need AuditLog dot Read dot
All and Directory dot Read dot All.

8
00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:29.275
Those are the only two
permissions a real run would need.

9
00:00:29.275 --> 00:00:31.725
Step two checks the program's register.

10
00:00:31.725 --> 00:00:36.998
It comes back with zero findings, zero
warnings and zero information items,

11
00:00:36.998 --> 00:00:41.675
and an exit code of zero, so the
register's shape passes every W R rule.

12
00:00:41.675 --> 00:00:43.805
That's the precondition for the scan:

13
00:00:43.805 --> 00:00:47.690
a register you've checked is one
you can test the audit log against.
